## 4. Features & Benefits

| Feature (what it does) | Benefit (how my life gets better) | MVP or Later? |
|---|---|---|
| **Client-Side WASM Engine (FFmpeg.wasm)** | Compresses audio, video, and photos directly in the browser. | MVP |
| **Discord & Cloud Target Presets** | one-click targets (e.g., "Fit under 25 MB Discord limit" or "50% Storage Reduction") so I don't have to guess bitrates or resolutions. | MVP |
| **Multi-Format Batch Support** | Drag and drop multiple different files across different media types (MP4, MOV, MP3, WAV, PNG, JPG) | MVP |
| **Custom Bitrate & Quality Sliders** | Manual slider controls for tuning output file sizes and audio/video compression levels when automated presets aren't enough. | Later |
| **Before/After Media Preview & Quality Comparison** | Preview of visual quality and estimated export file size before downloading. | Later |

**MVP (2–3 features):**
- **Client-Side WASM Engine:** Full in-browser processing for zero server uploads, total privacy, and high performance.
- **Target File Size Presets:** One-click options designed specifically around Discord's 25 MB free limit and cloud storage saving.
- **Drag-and-Drop Multi-Format Input:** Seamless drag-and-drop support for common video, audio, and image formats.

**Later:**
- Custom compression controls (bitrate, resolution scaling, frame rate adjustments).
- Before/after preview player to show media quality prior to download.
- Custom preset creation (saving a user-defined "Quick Audio Demo" setting).

**Not doing:**
- Remote server hosting or cloud processing (keeps architecture 100% local, free, and private).
- Built-in video editing capabilities like trimming, cropping, or splitting.
- Account creation, user login systems, or audio file sharing capabilities.

