## 5. Tech Stack

### Front end
- **Surface:** Web application
- **Tools:** React, Vite, TS, FFMPEG, WebAssembly
- **Why:** Whenever I am on my PC a browser is usually open, especially when dealing with google drive/photos

### Back end
| Piece | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Server / API | Client-only (Static Site / Next.js SPA) | All compression runs locally via WebAssembly; no server backend neccesary. |
| Data storage | Local Browser Memory | Stores temporary processed files locally in memory until downloaded. |
| Hosting / deploy | GitHub Pages | Free, static deployment with high reliability and quick setup. |

### Architecture sketch

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    U["User"] --> FE["Front End: Next.js + React UI"]
    FE --> WASM["Local Engine: FFmpeg.wasm (Client-Side)"]
    WASM --> MEM[("Browser Memory / Blob Storage")]
```

